Technique: T1105
Tactic: Command and Control
Data Source: ProcessEvents

Behavior:
`curl` is used to retrieve resources from a remote HTTP/HTTPS location.

Detection Logic:
Detects `curl` execution where the command line contains an HTTP or HTTPS URL.

False Positives:
Legitimate software installation, system administration, API requests, development, and CI/CD activity.

Severity:
Medium

Detection:
ProcessEvents
| where process_name =~ "curl"
| where process_commandline has_any ("http://", "https://")
| project timestamp, hostname, process_name, process_commandline

